node_modules/

# Holds the bearer token the daemon refuses to start without.
#
# Widened to every `.env.*` variant, with `.env.example` exempted, because
# `.dockerignore` already denies `**/.env` and `**/.env.*` and the two disagreeing
# is how a `.env.production` ends up tracked while the image correctly refuses it.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Nothing in this repository generates these, which is the point: a key or a
# certificate appearing in a working tree is a mistake, and it should not be one
# `git add -A` away from being public and permanent.
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.crt
*.cer
id_rsa*
id_ed25519*

# npm and pnpm write registry auth tokens here, and `pnpm` is this repository's
# package manager. Nothing tracked needs one — every resolution in
# `pnpm-lock.yaml` is the public registry — so a file appearing at all is either
# a credential or a mistake, and both want the same treatment.
.npmrc

*.log
.DS_Store

# The event log holds full agent transcripts and every file diff. Insurance
# against someone pointing REEMOAT_DB at the repo.
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# Local agent tooling, not part of this project.
#
# `.claude/rules/` is tracked on purpose — it is this repository's own
# documentation, loaded by path. Everything else under `.claude/` is one
# person's harness configuration, and `settings.json` in particular registers
# hooks that *execute* on somebody else's machine the moment they open a
# checkout. This repository publishes an install script and a SECURITY.md; it
# does not also run code on a contributor before they have read the diff.
.gstack/
.claude/settings.json
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/*.local.json
.claude/hooks/
.claude/agents/

# Build output. The control plane serves packages/web/dist when it is there and
# says how to build it when it is not, so there is nothing to check in.
dist/

# A packaged plugin. `docs/PLUGINS.md` tells somebody to build one in the
# repository root — `tar -czf board.tgz -C plugins/board .` — so the documented
# first step leaves an untracked archive beside the tree it was built from.
*.tgz

# The native shell's build tree and its generated projects.
#
# `target/` is **2.9 GB** after one `cargo check` on this checkout, which is why
# this is not only hygiene: `scripts/docscheck.ts` walks the working tree rather
# than `git ls-files`, so it would read every `.json` fingerprint in there into the
# symbol corpus — slow, and one dependency away from making a stale symbol
# "resolve" and inverting the ratchet that catches broken pointers. `SKIP_DIR` in
# that driver is the half that actually holds; this is the half that keeps the tree
# clean and keeps `gitleaks --no-git` from scanning build output.
#
# `gen/schemas/` is written by `tauri-build` on every compile from the capability
# files. `gen/android` and `gen/apple` are **not** matched here on purpose: those
# are generated once by `tauri android init` / `tauri ios init` and then edited and
# committed, the way a checked-in Xcode project is.
packages/native/src-tauri/target/
packages/native/src-tauri/gen/schemas/
